t(3, 265, """The post is not for those who shave the beard and the moustache

The post is for those who keep the beard and strip off the moustache, which is something the Prophet ﷺ never did in his life at all. Never. Absolutely. Not at all.

The Prophet ﷺ was described in the books of Sunnah and the Prophetic shama'il as having a moustache, and he was not without one. The moustache is part of men's natural constitution, and the Prophet ﷺ was the most perfect of people in form and character.

The existence of the moustache and its description are established in the narrations in several ways:

1. The verbal description in the books of shama'il
It came in some narrations describing the cheeks and mouth of the Prophet ﷺ that he was "ashnab". In the language of the Arabs, shanab is used for one who has a thin, defined moustache. And as came in the hadith of Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, describing the grey hair of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: "The whiteness was only in his lower lip tuft, in the 'moustache', and in his head a few strands" (narrated by Imam Ahmad and authenticated by the verifiers), which proves the existence of the moustache.

2. The practical Sunnah reported from him

The mass-transmitted authentic hadiths in which he ﷺ commands taking from the moustache, such as his saying: "Whoever does not take from his moustache is not of us", and his saying: "Trim the moustaches closely", are in themselves proof that he had a moustache, since the Prophet ﷺ is the first to follow the rules of the fitrah that he commands the Muslims.

3. How he trimmed his moustache

As for its size and shape, it is reported in the Sunnah that it was trimmed and carefully clipped, including:

He would take from his moustache until the whiteness of the skin beneath it showed and his upper lip appeared.

It is reported that he took from its two ends (the two sides of the moustache that slope down to the corners of the lip) so that the moustache hair would not grow long or hang over his noble mouth.

Therefore the Prophet ﷺ did not leave his moustache long and thick, nor did he uproot it completely by shaving with a razor, as thousands of religious people sadly do today; rather he had a moustache described as orderly, trimmed and perfectly clean, in keeping with the qualities of the fitrah with which he was sent, and he ﷺ is innocent of this aberrant practice in appearance and form; we seek refuge in Allah from such a repulsive sight.""")

h(3, 2100, """Once again
Removing the moustache is wrong
The Prophet never did that at all""")

